      "clozeText": "Learning about exploring sung sot cave in ha long bay offers secondary school students meaningful insights into our culture and environment. In Ha Long Bay, local people take great pride in preserving their natural surroundings and (23) ________. Every morning, residents and visitors can breathe the pure (24) ________ while admiring the beautiful landscape. To keep this destination attractive, all tourists (25) ________ follow local rules and avoid littering. Furthermore, spending time participating in kayaking helps young people develop valuable life (26) ________. In summary, visiting this destination leaves an unforgettable (27) ________ in everyone's memory.",
      "readingText": "Exploring Sung Sot Cave in Ha Long Bay represents one of the most beloved cultural and geographical highlights associated with Ha Long Bay. Covering a picturesque territory, this destination welcomes thousands of visitors who come to experience Sung Sot Cave and emerald water. During festive seasons or sunny weekends, families gather to take part in kayaking, creating a warm and vibrant atmosphere. Local authorities and community volunteers work tirelessly to maintain public cleanliness, install solar lighting, and protect stalactites. Moreover, friendly local residents always greet newcomers with sincere hospitality, offering helpful directions and traditional specialities. Preserving these cherished values ensures that younger generations continue to appreciate the cultural heritage and natural wonders of our homeland.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nLearning about exploring sung sot cave in ha long bay offers secondary school students meaningful insights into our culture and environment. In Ha Long Bay, local people take great pride in preserving their natural surroundings and (23) ________. Every morning, residents and visitors can breathe the pure (24) ________ while admiring the beautiful landscape. To keep this destination attractive, all tourists (25) ________ follow local rules and avoid littering. Furthermore, spending time participating in kayaking helps young people develop valuable life (26) ________. In summary, visiting this destination leaves an unforgettable (27) ________ in everyone's memory.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nExploring Sung Sot Cave in Ha Long Bay represents one of the most beloved cultural and geographical highlights associated with Ha Long Bay. Covering a picturesque territory, this destination welcomes thousands of visitors who come to experience Sung Sot Cave and emerald water. During festive seasons or sunny weekends, families gather to take part in kayaking, creating a warm and vibrant atmosphere. Local authorities and community volunteers work tirelessly to maintain public cleanliness, install solar lighting, and protect stalactites. Moreover, friendly local residents always greet newcomers with sincere hospitality, offering helpful directions and traditional specialities. Preserving these cherished values ensures that younger generations continue to appreciate the cultural heritage and natural wonders of our homeland.",
