      "audioScript": "What cultural heritage or culinary topic are you reviewing for English class?\nI am presenting about Traditional Water Puppet Theatre in Ha Noi at Thang Long Theatre.\nWhat is the most remarkable aspect of this tradition?\nEveryone appreciates wooden puppets on water and enjoys watching puppet plays.\nHow does it reflect the cultural identity of our people?\nIt highlights traditional folk orchestra and showcases the authentic value of bamboo screen.\nThat is wonderful! You will definitely achieve a high grade for your presentation.",
      "clozeText": "Vietnamese culture is celebrated worldwide for its artistic depth and culinary excellence. When studying traditional water puppet theatre in ha noi, students discover how Thang Long Theatre preserves authentic (23) ________. For example, mastering watching puppet plays requires great dedication and (24) ________ from learners. Many traditional recipes and art forms are (25) ________ from what we find in western cultures. In addition, visitors can taste or admire wooden puppets on water, which reflects the rich spirit of our (26) ________. Therefore, protecting these timeless treasures guarantees a strong sense of cultural (27) ________.",
      "readingText": "Traditional Water Puppet Theatre in Ha Noi represents an invaluable facet of Vietnamese cultural heritage, deeply anchored in Thang Long Theatre. Over many centuries, generations of craftsmen and scholars have refined wooden puppets on water and traditional folk orchestra, creating a national icon. Both domestic visitors and foreign tourists are captivated when participating in watching puppet plays, praising the skill and hospitality of locals. Cultural educators actively safeguard bamboo screen to ensure ancient techniques remain vibrant in the modern era. Whether enjoying aromatic regional specialties or admiring historic architecture, learners gain profound respect for national history. By cherishing and promoting these traditions, young Vietnamese students foster international friendship and cultural preservation.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nVietnamese culture is celebrated worldwide for its artistic depth and culinary excellence. When studying traditional water puppet theatre in ha noi, students discover how Thang Long Theatre preserves authentic (23) ________. For example, mastering watching puppet plays requires great dedication and (24) ________ from learners. Many traditional recipes and art forms are (25) ________ from what we find in western cultures. In addition, visitors can taste or admire wooden puppets on water, which reflects the rich spirit of our (26) ________. Therefore, protecting these timeless treasures guarantees a strong sense of cultural (27) ________.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nTraditional Water Puppet Theatre in Ha Noi represents an invaluable facet of Vietnamese cultural heritage, deeply anchored in Thang Long Theatre. Over many centuries, generations of craftsmen and scholars have refined wooden puppets on water and traditional folk orchestra, creating a national icon. Both domestic visitors and foreign tourists are captivated when participating in watching puppet plays, praising the skill and hospitality of locals. Cultural educators actively safeguard bamboo screen to ensure ancient techniques remain vibrant in the modern era. Whether enjoying aromatic regional specialties or admiring historic architecture, learners gain profound respect for national history. By cherishing and promoting these traditions, young Vietnamese students foster international friendship and cultural preservation.",
