      "audioUrl": "",
      "audioScript": "What cultural heritage or culinary topic are you reviewing for English class?\nI am presenting about Dong Ho Folk Painting Craft in Bac Ninh at Dong Ho village.\nWhat is the most remarkable aspect of this tradition?\nEveryone appreciates natural woodblock prints and enjoys painting folk designs.\nHow does it reflect the cultural identity of our people?\nIt highlights scallop shell paper and showcases the authentic value of traditional artisan.\nThat is wonderful! You will definitely achieve a high grade for your presentation.",
      "clozeText": "Vietnamese culture is celebrated worldwide for its artistic depth and culinary excellence. When studying dong ho folk painting craft in bac ninh, students discover how Dong Ho village preserves authentic (23) ________. For example, mastering painting folk designs requires great dedication and (24) ________ from learners. Many traditional recipes and art forms are (25) ________ from what we find in western cultures. In addition, visitors can taste or admire natural woodblock prints, which reflects the rich spirit of our (26) ________. Therefore, protecting these timeless treasures guarantees a strong sense of cultural (27) ________.",
      "readingText": "Dong Ho Folk Painting Craft in Bac Ninh represents an invaluable facet of Vietnamese cultural heritage, deeply anchored in Dong Ho village. Over many centuries, generations of craftsmen and scholars have refined natural woodblock prints and scallop shell paper, creating a national icon. Both domestic visitors and foreign tourists are captivated when participating in painting folk designs, praising the skill and hospitality of locals. Cultural educators actively safeguard traditional artisan to ensure ancient techniques remain vibrant in the modern era. Whether enjoying aromatic regional specialties or admiring historic architecture, learners gain profound respect for national history. By cherishing and promoting these traditions, young Vietnamese students foster international friendship and cultural preservation.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nVietnamese culture is celebrated worldwide for its artistic depth and culinary excellence. When studying dong ho folk painting craft in bac ninh, students discover how Dong Ho village preserves authentic (23) ________. For example, mastering painting folk designs requires great dedication and (24) ________ from learners. Many traditional recipes and art forms are (25) ________ from what we find in western cultures. In addition, visitors can taste or admire natural woodblock prints, which reflects the rich spirit of our (26) ________. Therefore, protecting these timeless treasures guarantees a strong sense of cultural (27) ________.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nDong Ho Folk Painting Craft in Bac Ninh represents an invaluable facet of Vietnamese cultural heritage, deeply anchored in Dong Ho village. Over many centuries, generations of craftsmen and scholars have refined natural woodblock prints and scallop shell paper, creating a national icon. Both domestic visitors and foreign tourists are captivated when participating in painting folk designs, praising the skill and hospitality of locals. Cultural educators actively safeguard traditional artisan to ensure ancient techniques remain vibrant in the modern era. Whether enjoying aromatic regional specialties or admiring historic architecture, learners gain profound respect for national history. By cherishing and promoting these traditions, young Vietnamese students foster international friendship and cultural preservation.",
      "writingRubric": "Bố cục rõ ràng (0.25đ) - Ngữ pháp & Từ vựng chính xác (0.5đ) - Tính liên kết mạch lạc (0.25đ)",
      "sampleWritingText": "Dong Ho Folk Painting Craft in Bac Ninh at Dong Ho village is one of my favourite cultural experiences. It showcases natural woodblock prints and reflects the profound wisdom of our ancestors. When engaging in painting folk designs, visitors discover how scallop shell paper has been preserved across generations. Furthermore, safeguarding traditional artisan helps younger people maintain a strong cultural identity. I am very proud of this Vietnamese heritage.",
