      "audioUrl": "",
      "audioScript": "What cultural heritage or culinary topic are you reviewing for English class?\nI am presenting about Cooking Traditional Crispy Spring Rolls (Nem Ran) at family kitchen.\nWhat is the most remarkable aspect of this tradition?\nEveryone appreciates crispy rice paper wrappers and enjoys frying golden rolls.\nHow does it reflect the cultural identity of our people?\nIt highlights minced pork and mushrooms and showcases the authentic value of sweet and sour dipping sauce.\nThat is wonderful! You will definitely achieve a high grade for your presentation.",
      "clozeText": "Vietnamese culture is celebrated worldwide for its artistic depth and culinary excellence. When studying cooking traditional crispy spring rolls (nem ran), students discover how family kitchen preserves authentic (23) ________. For example, mastering frying golden rolls requires great dedication and (24) ________ from learners. Many traditional recipes and art forms are (25) ________ from what we find in western cultures. In addition, visitors can taste or admire crispy rice paper wrappers, which reflects the rich spirit of our (26) ________. Therefore, protecting these timeless treasures guarantees a strong sense of cultural (27) ________.",
      "readingText": "Cooking Traditional Crispy Spring Rolls (Nem Ran) represents an invaluable facet of Vietnamese cultural heritage, deeply anchored in family kitchen. Over many centuries, generations of craftsmen and scholars have refined crispy rice paper wrappers and minced pork and mushrooms, creating a national icon. Both domestic visitors and foreign tourists are captivated when participating in frying golden rolls, praising the skill and hospitality of locals. Cultural educators actively safeguard sweet and sour dipping sauce to ensure ancient techniques remain vibrant in the modern era. Whether enjoying aromatic regional specialties or admiring historic architecture, learners gain profound respect for national history. By cherishing and promoting these traditions, young Vietnamese students foster international friendship and cultural preservation.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nVietnamese culture is celebrated worldwide for its artistic depth and culinary excellence. When studying cooking traditional crispy spring rolls (nem ran), students discover how family kitchen preserves authentic (23) ________. For example, mastering frying golden rolls requires great dedication and (24) ________ from learners. Many traditional recipes and art forms are (25) ________ from what we find in western cultures. In addition, visitors can taste or admire crispy rice paper wrappers, which reflects the rich spirit of our (26) ________. Therefore, protecting these timeless treasures guarantees a strong sense of cultural (27) ________.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nCooking Traditional Crispy Spring Rolls (Nem Ran) represents an invaluable facet of Vietnamese cultural heritage, deeply anchored in family kitchen. Over many centuries, generations of craftsmen and scholars have refined crispy rice paper wrappers and minced pork and mushrooms, creating a national icon. Both domestic visitors and foreign tourists are captivated when participating in frying golden rolls, praising the skill and hospitality of locals. Cultural educators actively safeguard sweet and sour dipping sauce to ensure ancient techniques remain vibrant in the modern era. Whether enjoying aromatic regional specialties or admiring historic architecture, learners gain profound respect for national history. By cherishing and promoting these traditions, young Vietnamese students foster international friendship and cultural preservation.",
      "writingRubric": "Bố cục rõ ràng (0.25đ) - Ngữ pháp & Từ vựng chính xác (0.5đ) - Tính liên kết mạch lạc (0.25đ)",
      "sampleWritingText": "Cooking Traditional Crispy Spring Rolls (Nem Ran) at family kitchen is one of my favourite cultural experiences. It showcases crispy rice paper wrappers and reflects the profound wisdom of our ancestors. When engaging in frying golden rolls, visitors discover how minced pork and mushrooms has been preserved across generations. Furthermore, safeguarding sweet and sour dipping sauce helps younger people maintain a strong cultural identity. I am very proud of this Vietnamese heritage.",
