      "audioScript": "What cultural heritage or culinary topic are you reviewing for English class?\nI am presenting about Preserving Heritage at Quoc Hoc Hue High School at Perfume River bank.\nWhat is the most remarkable aspect of this tradition?\nEveryone appreciates dark red school walls and enjoys attending history club.\nHow does it reflect the cultural identity of our people?\nIt highlights shaded tamarind trees and showcases the authentic value of commemorative plaque.\nThat is wonderful! You will definitely achieve a high grade for your presentation.",
      "clozeText": "Vietnamese culture is celebrated worldwide for its artistic depth and culinary excellence. When studying preserving heritage at quoc hoc hue high school, students discover how Perfume River bank preserves authentic (23) ________. For example, mastering attending history club requires great dedication and (24) ________ from learners. Many traditional recipes and art forms are (25) ________ from what we find in western cultures. In addition, visitors can taste or admire dark red school walls, which reflects the rich spirit of our (26) ________. Therefore, protecting these timeless treasures guarantees a strong sense of cultural (27) ________.",
      "readingText": "Preserving Heritage at Quoc Hoc Hue High School represents an invaluable facet of Vietnamese cultural heritage, deeply anchored in Perfume River bank. Over many centuries, generations of craftsmen and scholars have refined dark red school walls and shaded tamarind trees, creating a national icon. Both domestic visitors and foreign tourists are captivated when participating in attending history club, praising the skill and hospitality of locals. Cultural educators actively safeguard commemorative plaque to ensure ancient techniques remain vibrant in the modern era. Whether enjoying aromatic regional specialties or admiring historic architecture, learners gain profound respect for national history. By cherishing and promoting these traditions, young Vietnamese students foster international friendship and cultural preservation.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nVietnamese culture is celebrated worldwide for its artistic depth and culinary excellence. When studying preserving heritage at quoc hoc hue high school, students discover how Perfume River bank preserves authentic (23) ________. For example, mastering attending history club requires great dedication and (24) ________ from learners. Many traditional recipes and art forms are (25) ________ from what we find in western cultures. In addition, visitors can taste or admire dark red school walls, which reflects the rich spirit of our (26) ________. Therefore, protecting these timeless treasures guarantees a strong sense of cultural (27) ________.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nPreserving Heritage at Quoc Hoc Hue High School represents an invaluable facet of Vietnamese cultural heritage, deeply anchored in Perfume River bank. Over many centuries, generations of craftsmen and scholars have refined dark red school walls and shaded tamarind trees, creating a national icon. Both domestic visitors and foreign tourists are captivated when participating in attending history club, praising the skill and hospitality of locals. Cultural educators actively safeguard commemorative plaque to ensure ancient techniques remain vibrant in the modern era. Whether enjoying aromatic regional specialties or admiring historic architecture, learners gain profound respect for national history. By cherishing and promoting these traditions, young Vietnamese students foster international friendship and cultural preservation.",
