      "audioScript": "What cultural tradition or lifestyle are you discussing in English class?\nI am presenting about The Unique Architecture of Tay Stilt Houses in Ha Giang at Ha Giang mountains.\nWhat is the most fascinating aspect of this custom?\nAnthropologists and participants are intrigued by lofty timber stilt houses and enjoy weaving traditional brocade.\nHow does it preserve cultural heritage or improve well-being?\nIt reinforces raised bamboo living platforms and honors the spiritual value of sacred ancestral altar.\nWonderful! That provides an insightful perspective on cultural diversity.",
      "clozeText": "Understanding diverse cultural customs and modern lifestyles enriches our appreciation of human society. In Ha Giang mountains, local communities take tremendous pride in preserving lofty timber stilt houses and ancestral (23) ________. When participating in weaving traditional brocade, young people cultivate respect, empathy, and social (24) ________. Although contemporary lifestyles are evolving rapidly, people (25) ________ remember their ancestral origins. Furthermore, integrating raised bamboo living platforms helps teenagers lead more meaningful and (26) ________ lives. In summary, cherishing sacred ancestral altar strengthens the bond between past heritage and future (27) ________.",
      "readingText": "The Unique Architecture of Tay Stilt Houses in Ha Giang exemplifies the profound richness of cultural diversity and community identity found in Ha Giang mountains. Rooted in centuries of history, this custom embodies lofty timber stilt houses and reflects raised bamboo living platforms, captivating observers worldwide. Communities who actively engage in weaving traditional brocade maintain strong interpersonal harmony and mutual assistance across generations. Cultural specialists emphasize sacred ancestral altar as a vital emblem that shields ancient wisdom from the pressures of globalization. Moreover, whether studying traditional ethnic practices or adopting conscious sustainable lifestyles, youths gain moral depth. By embracing ancestral heritage alongside modern progress, societies preserve their cultural soul while marching forward.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nUnderstanding diverse cultural customs and modern lifestyles enriches our appreciation of human society. In Ha Giang mountains, local communities take tremendous pride in preserving lofty timber stilt houses and ancestral (23) ________. When participating in weaving traditional brocade, young people cultivate respect, empathy, and social (24) ________. Although contemporary lifestyles are evolving rapidly, people (25) ________ remember their ancestral origins. Furthermore, integrating raised bamboo living platforms helps teenagers lead more meaningful and (26) ________ lives. In summary, cherishing sacred ancestral altar strengthens the bond between past heritage and future (27) ________.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nThe Unique Architecture of Tay Stilt Houses in Ha Giang exemplifies the profound richness of cultural diversity and community identity found in Ha Giang mountains. Rooted in centuries of history, this custom embodies lofty timber stilt houses and reflects raised bamboo living platforms, captivating observers worldwide. Communities who actively engage in weaving traditional brocade maintain strong interpersonal harmony and mutual assistance across generations. Cultural specialists emphasize sacred ancestral altar as a vital emblem that shields ancient wisdom from the pressures of globalization. Moreover, whether studying traditional ethnic practices or adopting conscious sustainable lifestyles, youths gain moral depth. By embracing ancestral heritage alongside modern progress, societies preserve their cultural soul while marching forward.",
      "writingRubric": "Bố cục rõ ràng (0.25đ) - Ngữ pháp & Từ vựng chính xác (0.5đ) - Tính liên kết mạch lạc (0.25đ)",
      "sampleWritingText": "In my opinion, The Unique Architecture of Tay Stilt Houses in Ha Giang is an extraordinary cultural treasure. Located in Ha Giang mountains, it embodies lofty timber stilt houses and illustrates how communities harmoniously interact with their environment. Practicing weaving traditional brocade instills profound moral values and preserves raised bamboo living platforms. Moreover, honoring sacred ancestral altar reinforces our ancestral roots. I believe youth should actively champion the preservation of this cherished heritage.",
