      "audioScript": "What cultural tradition or lifestyle are you discussing in English class?\nI am presenting about Terraced Rice Fields of Mu Cang Chai in Golden Season at Yen Bai mountain slopes.\nWhat is the most fascinating aspect of this custom?\nAnthropologists and participants are intrigued by stepped golden rice paddies and enjoy reaping golden paddy ears.\nHow does it preserve cultural heritage or improve well-being?\nIt reinforces scenic valley panoramas and honors the spiritual value of wooden rice thresher.\nWonderful! That provides an insightful perspective on cultural diversity.",
      "clozeText": "Understanding diverse cultural customs and modern lifestyles enriches our appreciation of human society. In Yen Bai mountain slopes, local communities take tremendous pride in preserving stepped golden rice paddies and ancestral (23) ________. When participating in reaping golden paddy ears, young people cultivate respect, empathy, and social (24) ________. Although contemporary lifestyles are evolving rapidly, people (25) ________ remember their ancestral origins. Furthermore, integrating scenic valley panoramas helps teenagers lead more meaningful and (26) ________ lives. In summary, cherishing wooden rice thresher strengthens the bond between past heritage and future (27) ________.",
      "readingText": "Terraced Rice Fields of Mu Cang Chai in Golden Season exemplifies the profound richness of cultural diversity and community identity found in Yen Bai mountain slopes. Rooted in centuries of history, this custom embodies stepped golden rice paddies and reflects scenic valley panoramas, captivating observers worldwide. Communities who actively engage in reaping golden paddy ears maintain strong interpersonal harmony and mutual assistance across generations. Cultural specialists emphasize wooden rice thresher as a vital emblem that shields ancient wisdom from the pressures of globalization. Moreover, whether studying traditional ethnic practices or adopting conscious sustainable lifestyles, youths gain moral depth. By embracing ancestral heritage alongside modern progress, societies preserve their cultural soul while marching forward.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nUnderstanding diverse cultural customs and modern lifestyles enriches our appreciation of human society. In Yen Bai mountain slopes, local communities take tremendous pride in preserving stepped golden rice paddies and ancestral (23) ________. When participating in reaping golden paddy ears, young people cultivate respect, empathy, and social (24) ________. Although contemporary lifestyles are evolving rapidly, people (25) ________ remember their ancestral origins. Furthermore, integrating scenic valley panoramas helps teenagers lead more meaningful and (26) ________ lives. In summary, cherishing wooden rice thresher strengthens the bond between past heritage and future (27) ________.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nTerraced Rice Fields of Mu Cang Chai in Golden Season exemplifies the profound richness of cultural diversity and community identity found in Yen Bai mountain slopes. Rooted in centuries of history, this custom embodies stepped golden rice paddies and reflects scenic valley panoramas, captivating observers worldwide. Communities who actively engage in reaping golden paddy ears maintain strong interpersonal harmony and mutual assistance across generations. Cultural specialists emphasize wooden rice thresher as a vital emblem that shields ancient wisdom from the pressures of globalization. Moreover, whether studying traditional ethnic practices or adopting conscious sustainable lifestyles, youths gain moral depth. By embracing ancestral heritage alongside modern progress, societies preserve their cultural soul while marching forward.",
      "writingRubric": "Bố cục rõ ràng (0.25đ) - Ngữ pháp & Từ vựng chính xác (0.5đ) - Tính liên kết mạch lạc (0.25đ)",
      "sampleWritingText": "In my opinion, Terraced Rice Fields of Mu Cang Chai in Golden Season is an extraordinary cultural treasure. Located in Yen Bai mountain slopes, it embodies stepped golden rice paddies and illustrates how communities harmoniously interact with their environment. Practicing reaping golden paddy ears instills profound moral values and preserves scenic valley panoramas. Moreover, honoring wooden rice thresher reinforces our ancestral roots. I believe youth should actively champion the preservation of this cherished heritage.",
