      "audioUrl": "",
      "audioScript": "What cultural tradition or lifestyle are you discussing in English class?\nI am presenting about The Cham Pottery Tradition of Bau Truc Village at Ninh Thuan province.\nWhat is the most fascinating aspect of this custom?\nAnthropologists and participants are intrigued by hand-molded red clay pots and enjoy shaping clay without wheels.\nHow does it preserve cultural heritage or improve well-being?\nIt reinforces outdoor straw kiln firing and honors the spiritual value of artisan pottery stamp.\nWonderful! That provides an insightful perspective on cultural diversity.",
      "clozeText": "Understanding diverse cultural customs and modern lifestyles enriches our appreciation of human society. In Ninh Thuan province, local communities take tremendous pride in preserving hand-molded red clay pots and ancestral (23) ________. When participating in shaping clay without wheels, young people cultivate respect, empathy, and social (24) ________. Although contemporary lifestyles are evolving rapidly, people (25) ________ remember their ancestral origins. Furthermore, integrating outdoor straw kiln firing helps teenagers lead more meaningful and (26) ________ lives. In summary, cherishing artisan pottery stamp strengthens the bond between past heritage and future (27) ________.",
      "readingText": "The Cham Pottery Tradition of Bau Truc Village exemplifies the profound richness of cultural diversity and community identity found in Ninh Thuan province. Rooted in centuries of history, this custom embodies hand-molded red clay pots and reflects outdoor straw kiln firing, captivating observers worldwide. Communities who actively engage in shaping clay without wheels maintain strong interpersonal harmony and mutual assistance across generations. Cultural specialists emphasize artisan pottery stamp as a vital emblem that shields ancient wisdom from the pressures of globalization. Moreover, whether studying traditional ethnic practices or adopting conscious sustainable lifestyles, youths gain moral depth. By embracing ancestral heritage alongside modern progress, societies preserve their cultural soul while marching forward.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nUnderstanding diverse cultural customs and modern lifestyles enriches our appreciation of human society. In Ninh Thuan province, local communities take tremendous pride in preserving hand-molded red clay pots and ancestral (23) ________. When participating in shaping clay without wheels, young people cultivate respect, empathy, and social (24) ________. Although contemporary lifestyles are evolving rapidly, people (25) ________ remember their ancestral origins. Furthermore, integrating outdoor straw kiln firing helps teenagers lead more meaningful and (26) ________ lives. In summary, cherishing artisan pottery stamp strengthens the bond between past heritage and future (27) ________.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nThe Cham Pottery Tradition of Bau Truc Village exemplifies the profound richness of cultural diversity and community identity found in Ninh Thuan province. Rooted in centuries of history, this custom embodies hand-molded red clay pots and reflects outdoor straw kiln firing, captivating observers worldwide. Communities who actively engage in shaping clay without wheels maintain strong interpersonal harmony and mutual assistance across generations. Cultural specialists emphasize artisan pottery stamp as a vital emblem that shields ancient wisdom from the pressures of globalization. Moreover, whether studying traditional ethnic practices or adopting conscious sustainable lifestyles, youths gain moral depth. By embracing ancestral heritage alongside modern progress, societies preserve their cultural soul while marching forward.",
      "writingRubric": "Bố cục rõ ràng (0.25đ) - Ngữ pháp & Từ vựng chính xác (0.5đ) - Tính liên kết mạch lạc (0.25đ)",
      "sampleWritingText": "In my opinion, The Cham Pottery Tradition of Bau Truc Village is an extraordinary cultural treasure. Located in Ninh Thuan province, it embodies hand-molded red clay pots and illustrates how communities harmoniously interact with their environment. Practicing shaping clay without wheels instills profound moral values and preserves outdoor straw kiln firing. Moreover, honoring artisan pottery stamp reinforces our ancestral roots. I believe youth should actively champion the preservation of this cherished heritage.",
