      "audioUrl": "",
      "audioScript": "What historical milestone or wonder of Viet Nam are you presenting today?\nI am presenting about The Architectural Grandeur of Hue Imperial Citadel at Perfume River citadel.\nWhat is the most remarkable feature of this topic?\nHistorians and travelers are captivated by massive brick bastion walls and intrigued by touring the Forbidden Purple City.\nHow does it illustrate Viet Nam's heritage or rapid modernization?\nIt highlights intricate dragon carved throne and demonstrates the enduring value of Ngo Mon imperial gate.\nOutstanding! Your talk provides deep historical depth and national pride.",
      "clozeText": "Reflecting on the past and appreciating our national wonders allows teenagers to grasp how far society has progressed. In Perfume River citadel, historians and architects have meticulously studied massive brick bastion walls to document our cultural (23) ________. Over recent decades, Viet Nam has transformed from a war-torn agricultural land into a dynamic (24) ________. Older generations often remember when people (25) ________ rely on rudimentary tools and public tramways. By participating in touring the Forbidden Purple City, youths develop a profound respect for their ancestors' resilience and (26) ________. In conclusion, preserving Ngo Mon imperial gate guarantees that progress remains rooted in our timeless national (27) ________.",
      "readingText": "The Architectural Grandeur of Hue Imperial Citadel serves as an eloquent testament to the rich historical journey and natural magnificence associated with Perfume River citadel. Throughout decades of change, massive brick bastion walls and intricate dragon carved throne have stood as powerful symbols of Vietnamese perseverance and artistic mastery. Scholars and travelers who engage in touring the Forbidden Purple City gain intimate knowledge of how socio-economic shifts have reshaped daily existence. Preservationists and urban planners actively protect Ngo Mon imperial gate to strike a balance between modernization and historical integrity. Whether exploring colossal karst caverns or examining twentieth-century communal traditions, learners cultivate patriotic pride. Understanding these triumphs and memories empowers ninth graders to become enlightened, forward-looking global citizens.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nReflecting on the past and appreciating our national wonders allows teenagers to grasp how far society has progressed. In Perfume River citadel, historians and architects have meticulously studied massive brick bastion walls to document our cultural (23) ________. Over recent decades, Viet Nam has transformed from a war-torn agricultural land into a dynamic (24) ________. Older generations often remember when people (25) ________ rely on rudimentary tools and public tramways. By participating in touring the Forbidden Purple City, youths develop a profound respect for their ancestors' resilience and (26) ________. In conclusion, preserving Ngo Mon imperial gate guarantees that progress remains rooted in our timeless national (27) ________.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nThe Architectural Grandeur of Hue Imperial Citadel serves as an eloquent testament to the rich historical journey and natural magnificence associated with Perfume River citadel. Throughout decades of change, massive brick bastion walls and intricate dragon carved throne have stood as powerful symbols of Vietnamese perseverance and artistic mastery. Scholars and travelers who engage in touring the Forbidden Purple City gain intimate knowledge of how socio-economic shifts have reshaped daily existence. Preservationists and urban planners actively protect Ngo Mon imperial gate to strike a balance between modernization and historical integrity. Whether exploring colossal karst caverns or examining twentieth-century communal traditions, learners cultivate patriotic pride. Understanding these triumphs and memories empowers ninth graders to become enlightened, forward-looking global citizens.",
      "writingRubric": "Bố cục rõ ràng (0.25đ) - Ngữ pháp & Từ vựng chính xác (0.5đ) - Tính liên kết mạch lạc (0.25đ)",
      "sampleWritingText": "In my opinion, The Architectural Grandeur of Hue Imperial Citadel offers a profound window into our nation's history. Located in Perfume River citadel, it commemorates massive brick bastion walls and reflects the incredible resilience of previous generations. Reflecting on touring the Forbidden Purple City helps modern teenagers appreciate contemporary privileges while honoring intricate dragon carved throne. Furthermore, safeguarding Ngo Mon imperial gate preserves our sacred national soul amidst rapid globalization. I am immensely proud of Viet Nam's historical legacy.",
