      "audioScript": "What historical milestone or wonder of Viet Nam are you presenting today?\nI am presenting about The My Son Sanctuary: Ancient Cham Religious Architecture at Quang Nam forest valley.\nWhat is the most remarkable feature of this topic?\nHistorians and travelers are captivated by burnt red clay brick towers and intrigued by admiring ancient Cham masonry.\nHow does it illustrate Viet Nam's heritage or rapid modernization?\nIt highlights delicate Shiva and Apsara reliefs and demonstrates the enduring value of sacred inner sanctuary.\nOutstanding! Your talk provides deep historical depth and national pride.",
      "clozeText": "Reflecting on the past and appreciating our national wonders allows teenagers to grasp how far society has progressed. In Quang Nam forest valley, historians and architects have meticulously studied burnt red clay brick towers to document our cultural (23) ________. Over recent decades, Viet Nam has transformed from a war-torn agricultural land into a dynamic (24) ________. Older generations often remember when people (25) ________ rely on rudimentary tools and public tramways. By participating in admiring ancient Cham masonry, youths develop a profound respect for their ancestors' resilience and (26) ________. In conclusion, preserving sacred inner sanctuary guarantees that progress remains rooted in our timeless national (27) ________.",
      "readingText": "The My Son Sanctuary: Ancient Cham Religious Architecture serves as an eloquent testament to the rich historical journey and natural magnificence associated with Quang Nam forest valley. Throughout decades of change, burnt red clay brick towers and delicate Shiva and Apsara reliefs have stood as powerful symbols of Vietnamese perseverance and artistic mastery. Scholars and travelers who engage in admiring ancient Cham masonry gain intimate knowledge of how socio-economic shifts have reshaped daily existence. Preservationists and urban planners actively protect sacred inner sanctuary to strike a balance between modernization and historical integrity. Whether exploring colossal karst caverns or examining twentieth-century communal traditions, learners cultivate patriotic pride. Understanding these triumphs and memories empowers ninth graders to become enlightened, forward-looking global citizens.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nReflecting on the past and appreciating our national wonders allows teenagers to grasp how far society has progressed. In Quang Nam forest valley, historians and architects have meticulously studied burnt red clay brick towers to document our cultural (23) ________. Over recent decades, Viet Nam has transformed from a war-torn agricultural land into a dynamic (24) ________. Older generations often remember when people (25) ________ rely on rudimentary tools and public tramways. By participating in admiring ancient Cham masonry, youths develop a profound respect for their ancestors' resilience and (26) ________. In conclusion, preserving sacred inner sanctuary guarantees that progress remains rooted in our timeless national (27) ________.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nThe My Son Sanctuary: Ancient Cham Religious Architecture serves as an eloquent testament to the rich historical journey and natural magnificence associated with Quang Nam forest valley. Throughout decades of change, burnt red clay brick towers and delicate Shiva and Apsara reliefs have stood as powerful symbols of Vietnamese perseverance and artistic mastery. Scholars and travelers who engage in admiring ancient Cham masonry gain intimate knowledge of how socio-economic shifts have reshaped daily existence. Preservationists and urban planners actively protect sacred inner sanctuary to strike a balance between modernization and historical integrity. Whether exploring colossal karst caverns or examining twentieth-century communal traditions, learners cultivate patriotic pride. Understanding these triumphs and memories empowers ninth graders to become enlightened, forward-looking global citizens.",
