      "audioUrl": "",
      "audioScript": "What historical milestone or wonder of Viet Nam are you presenting today?\nI am presenting about Traditional Street Vendors and Rhythmic Selling Cries at Hanoi Old Quarter streets.\nWhat is the most remarkable feature of this topic?\nHistorians and travelers are captivated by balanced shoulder bamboo poles (don gánh) and intrigued by buying street breakfast.\nHow does it illustrate Viet Nam's heritage or rapid modernization?\nIt highlights warm sweet sticky rice (xôi) and demonstrates the enduring value of conical palm hat.\nOutstanding! Your talk provides deep historical depth and national pride.",
      "clozeText": "Reflecting on the past and appreciating our national wonders allows teenagers to grasp how far society has progressed. In Hanoi Old Quarter streets, historians and architects have meticulously studied balanced shoulder bamboo poles (don gánh) to document our cultural (23) ________. Over recent decades, Viet Nam has transformed from a war-torn agricultural land into a dynamic (24) ________. Older generations often remember when people (25) ________ rely on rudimentary tools and public tramways. By participating in buying street breakfast, youths develop a profound respect for their ancestors' resilience and (26) ________. In conclusion, preserving conical palm hat guarantees that progress remains rooted in our timeless national (27) ________.",
      "readingText": "Traditional Street Vendors and Rhythmic Selling Cries serves as an eloquent testament to the rich historical journey and natural magnificence associated with Hanoi Old Quarter streets. Throughout decades of change, balanced shoulder bamboo poles (don gánh) and warm sweet sticky rice (xôi) have stood as powerful symbols of Vietnamese perseverance and artistic mastery. Scholars and travelers who engage in buying street breakfast gain intimate knowledge of how socio-economic shifts have reshaped daily existence. Preservationists and urban planners actively protect conical palm hat to strike a balance between modernization and historical integrity. Whether exploring colossal karst caverns or examining twentieth-century communal traditions, learners cultivate patriotic pride. Understanding these triumphs and memories empowers ninth graders to become enlightened, forward-looking global citizens.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nReflecting on the past and appreciating our national wonders allows teenagers to grasp how far society has progressed. In Hanoi Old Quarter streets, historians and architects have meticulously studied balanced shoulder bamboo poles (don gánh) to document our cultural (23) ________. Over recent decades, Viet Nam has transformed from a war-torn agricultural land into a dynamic (24) ________. Older generations often remember when people (25) ________ rely on rudimentary tools and public tramways. By participating in buying street breakfast, youths develop a profound respect for their ancestors' resilience and (26) ________. In conclusion, preserving conical palm hat guarantees that progress remains rooted in our timeless national (27) ________.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nTraditional Street Vendors and Rhythmic Selling Cries serves as an eloquent testament to the rich historical journey and natural magnificence associated with Hanoi Old Quarter streets. Throughout decades of change, balanced shoulder bamboo poles (don gánh) and warm sweet sticky rice (xôi) have stood as powerful symbols of Vietnamese perseverance and artistic mastery. Scholars and travelers who engage in buying street breakfast gain intimate knowledge of how socio-economic shifts have reshaped daily existence. Preservationists and urban planners actively protect conical palm hat to strike a balance between modernization and historical integrity. Whether exploring colossal karst caverns or examining twentieth-century communal traditions, learners cultivate patriotic pride. Understanding these triumphs and memories empowers ninth graders to become enlightened, forward-looking global citizens.",
      "writingRubric": "Bố cục rõ ràng (0.25đ) - Ngữ pháp & Từ vựng chính xác (0.5đ) - Tính liên kết mạch lạc (0.25đ)",
      "sampleWritingText": "In my opinion, Traditional Street Vendors and Rhythmic Selling Cries offers a profound window into our nation's history. Located in Hanoi Old Quarter streets, it commemorates balanced shoulder bamboo poles (don gánh) and reflects the incredible resilience of previous generations. Reflecting on buying street breakfast helps modern teenagers appreciate contemporary privileges while honoring warm sweet sticky rice (xôi). Furthermore, safeguarding conical palm hat preserves our sacred national soul amidst rapid globalization. I am immensely proud of Viet Nam's historical legacy.",
