      "audioScript": "What historical milestone or wonder of Viet Nam are you presenting today?\nI am presenting about Ba Be Freshwater Mountain Lake Biosphere at Bac Kan national park.\nWhat is the most remarkable feature of this topic?\nHistorians and travelers are captivated by pristine mountain lake waters and intrigued by canoeing through calm bays.\nHow does it illustrate Viet Nam's heritage or rapid modernization?\nIt highlights rare freshwater fish species and demonstrates the enduring value of Tay ethnic wooden stilt house.\nOutstanding! Your talk provides deep historical depth and national pride.",
      "clozeText": "Reflecting on the past and appreciating our national wonders allows teenagers to grasp how far society has progressed. In Bac Kan national park, historians and architects have meticulously studied pristine mountain lake waters to document our cultural (23) ________. Over recent decades, Viet Nam has transformed from a war-torn agricultural land into a dynamic (24) ________. Older generations often remember when people (25) ________ rely on rudimentary tools and public tramways. By participating in canoeing through calm bays, youths develop a profound respect for their ancestors' resilience and (26) ________. In conclusion, preserving Tay ethnic wooden stilt house guarantees that progress remains rooted in our timeless national (27) ________.",
      "readingText": "Ba Be Freshwater Mountain Lake Biosphere serves as an eloquent testament to the rich historical journey and natural magnificence associated with Bac Kan national park. Throughout decades of change, pristine mountain lake waters and rare freshwater fish species have stood as powerful symbols of Vietnamese perseverance and artistic mastery. Scholars and travelers who engage in canoeing through calm bays gain intimate knowledge of how socio-economic shifts have reshaped daily existence. Preservationists and urban planners actively protect Tay ethnic wooden stilt house to strike a balance between modernization and historical integrity. Whether exploring colossal karst caverns or examining twentieth-century communal traditions, learners cultivate patriotic pride. Understanding these triumphs and memories empowers ninth graders to become enlightened, forward-looking global citizens.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nReflecting on the past and appreciating our national wonders allows teenagers to grasp how far society has progressed. In Bac Kan national park, historians and architects have meticulously studied pristine mountain lake waters to document our cultural (23) ________. Over recent decades, Viet Nam has transformed from a war-torn agricultural land into a dynamic (24) ________. Older generations often remember when people (25) ________ rely on rudimentary tools and public tramways. By participating in canoeing through calm bays, youths develop a profound respect for their ancestors' resilience and (26) ________. In conclusion, preserving Tay ethnic wooden stilt house guarantees that progress remains rooted in our timeless national (27) ________.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nBa Be Freshwater Mountain Lake Biosphere serves as an eloquent testament to the rich historical journey and natural magnificence associated with Bac Kan national park. Throughout decades of change, pristine mountain lake waters and rare freshwater fish species have stood as powerful symbols of Vietnamese perseverance and artistic mastery. Scholars and travelers who engage in canoeing through calm bays gain intimate knowledge of how socio-economic shifts have reshaped daily existence. Preservationists and urban planners actively protect Tay ethnic wooden stilt house to strike a balance between modernization and historical integrity. Whether exploring colossal karst caverns or examining twentieth-century communal traditions, learners cultivate patriotic pride. Understanding these triumphs and memories empowers ninth graders to become enlightened, forward-looking global citizens.",
      "writingRubric": "Bố cục rõ ràng (0.25đ) - Ngữ pháp & Từ vựng chính xác (0.5đ) - Tính liên kết mạch lạc (0.25đ)",
      "sampleWritingText": "In my opinion, Ba Be Freshwater Mountain Lake Biosphere offers a profound window into our nation's history. Located in Bac Kan national park, it commemorates pristine mountain lake waters and reflects the incredible resilience of previous generations. Reflecting on canoeing through calm bays helps modern teenagers appreciate contemporary privileges while honoring rare freshwater fish species. Furthermore, safeguarding Tay ethnic wooden stilt house preserves our sacred national soul amidst rapid globalization. I am immensely proud of Viet Nam's historical legacy.",
